      "source": [
        "### Implementing Transfer Learning with MobileNetV2\n",
        "\n",
        "Transfer learning is a technique where a model pre-trained on a large dataset (like ImageNet) is reused as a starting point for a new task. This leverages the features learned by the pre-trained model, which are often general enough to be useful for various image-related tasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will use `MobileNetV2` as our pre-trained base model. `MobileNetV2` is a lightweight deep neural network designed for mobile and embedded vision applications, making it efficient.\n",
        "\n",
        "Our strategy will be:\n",
        "1.  **Load the pre-trained `MobileNetV2` model**: We'll load it without its top classification layer, as we will add our own.\n",
        "2.  **Freeze the base model**: This prevents the weights of the pre-trained layers from being updated during the initial training, preserving the learned features.\n",
        "3.  **Add a custom classification head**: We'll add new `Dense` layers on top of the frozen base model, which will be trained on our specific cats and dogs dataset.\n",
        "4.  **Compile the new model**: With a suitable optimizer and loss function.\n",
        "5.  **Train the model**: Only the newly added classification head will be trained initially."
      ]
    },
